FILE: vUX-carousel.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
Three separate problems. First, the autoplay setInterval started by start() was never
cleared, so a removed carousel went on calling nextSlide() forever. Second, the
transitionend listener was anonymous and the container's onmouseenter/onmouseleave/onclick
assignments were never cleared. Third, the nested TouchHandler was held in a var local to
initialize(), so nothing could reach it to tear it down.

The transitionend handler is now the named handleTransitionEnd, hoisted out of
initialize() along with the touch setup; touchHdr moved to instance scope; and destroy()
clears the interval, detaches everything, destroys the TouchHandler, removes the generated
control strip and strips the inline styles and data attributes from the viewport and
sliders. The shared 'carouselStyles' sheet is deliberately left in place because every
Carousel on the page shares that one data-id.

Separately, this file called 'new TouchHandler(container)' without importing it. Since
config.touchResponse defaults to true, that was the default path, and initialize() threw
'TouchHandler is not defined' on any page that did not explicitly disable touch. The
import is now present.

